.TH "ET\-RETICULUM" "1" "November 2026" ""
.SH NAME
et\-reticulum \- configure and start a Reticulum shared instance
.SH SYNOPSIS
\f[B]et\-reticulum\f[R]
.SH DESCRIPTION
\f[B]et\-reticulum\f[R] configures and starts a shared instance of the
Reticulum Network Stack (RNS) using the \f[B]rnsd\f[R] daemon.
.PP
The operator selects a configuration blueprint from the available
\f[CR]config.blueprint.*\f[R] files in \f[CR]\(ti/.reticulum\f[R].
The selected blueprint is used to create the active Reticulum
configuration at \f[CR]\(ti/.reticulum/config\f[R], replacing the
previous configuration.
.PP
If a supported radio is connected and detected, \f[B]et\-reticulum\f[R]
offers compatible modem choices based on the selected blueprint.
It then asks the operator to acknowledge that Reticulum uses
end\-to\-end encryption and to confirm that its use is legal locally.
.PP
Before starting Reticulum, the utility updates configuration values for
the operator\(cqs callsign, available interfaces, and RNode transmit
power.
It then starts the Reticulum daemon (\f[B]rnsd\f[R]).
.SH CONFIGURATION BLUEPRINTS
Configuration blueprints are an EmComm Tools feature, not a native
Reticulum concept.
They provide reference configurations for quickly deploying Reticulum
nodes in common operating scenarios.
.PP
Available blueprints are discovered in \f[CR]\(ti/.reticulum\f[R] and
presented in an interactive selection menu.
Each blueprint defines a reference configuration for a particular
deployment scenario.
.PP
The selected blueprint is used to generate the active Reticulum
configuration.
Make persistent changes to the blueprint rather than the active
\f[CR]config\f[R] file.
.PP
To create a custom blueprint, copy an existing blueprint that most
closely matches your requirements.
Save the new configuration in \f[CR]\(ti/.reticulum\f[R] as
\f[CR]config.blueprint.DESCRIPTIVE\-NAME\f[R] and modify it as needed.
Run \f[B]et\-reticulum\f[R] again to select the new blueprint.
.TP
\f[B]Internet Client Only Node\f[R]
Connects to the public Reticulum network over the Internet using a TCP
client interface.
The default configuration connects to \f[CR]rns.thetechprepper.com\f[R].
Recommended for first\-time users.
.TP
\f[B]Local Network Only Node\f[R]
Configures Reticulum to communicate only over the local network using
Wi\-Fi or Ethernet.
Recommended when a Reticulum Transport Node is available on the same
network or when communicating exclusively with other local Reticulum
users.
.TP
\f[B]Mercury Only Node\f[R]
Configures Reticulum for radio\-only operation using the Mercury HF
modem.
Requires a supported HF radio selected with \f[B]et\-radio\f[R] and
connected to EmComm Tools.
The Mercury modem starts automatically.
Reticulum uses end\-to\-end encryption; ensure its use is permitted in
your region.
.TP
\f[B]modem73 Only Node\f[R]
Configures Reticulum for radio\-only operation using the modem73 modem.
Requires a supported radio selected with \f[B]et\-radio\f[R] and
connected to EmComm Tools.
The modem73 modem starts automatically.
Reticulum uses end\-to\-end encryption; ensure its use is permitted in
your region.
.TP
\f[B]Packet Only Node\f[R]
Configures Reticulum for radio\-only packet operation using the Dire
Wolf TNC.
Requires a supported radio selected with \f[B]et\-radio\f[R] and
connected to EmComm Tools.
Dire Wolf starts automatically.
Reticulum uses end\-to\-end encryption; ensure its use is permitted in
your region.
.TP
\f[B]Permanent Transport Node\f[R]
Configures Reticulum as a Transport Node for continuous 24/7 operation
using multiple network interfaces, including local Wi\-Fi/Ethernet, a
TCP client connection to \f[CR]rns.thetechprepper.com\f[R], a supported
LoRa RNode (e.g., Heltec V4), and a Dire Wolf packet interface when a
supported radio is connected.
Radio interfaces are enabled when supported hardware is available.
Ensure that encryption is permitted in your region before using radio
links.
.TP
\f[B]RNode Only Node\f[R]
Configures Reticulum for radio\-only operation using an RNode.
Requires a supported LoRa radio connected to EmComm Tools and flashed
with RNode firmware.
.SH BLUEPRINT REPLACEMENT TOKENS
EmComm Tools automatically replaces the following tokens with values
based on detected hardware when a blueprint is selected.
.TP
\f[B]ET_RETICULUM_INTERFACE_AX25KISS_ENABLED\f[R]
Replaced with \f[CR]Yes\f[R] when EmComm Tools detects a connected
radio, or \f[CR]No\f[R] otherwise.
Typically used to enable or disable the Reticulum
\f[CR]AX25KISSInterface\f[R].
.TP
\f[B]ET_RETICULUM_INTERFACE_MERCURY_ENABLED\f[R]
Replaced with \f[CR]Yes\f[R] when EmComm Tools detects a connected,
supported HF radio, or \f[CR]No\f[R] otherwise.
Used to enable or disable the Mercury HF interface.
.TP
\f[B]ET_RETICULUM_INTERFACE_MODEM73_ENABLED\f[R]
Replaced with \f[CR]Yes\f[R] when EmComm Tools detects a connected,
supported radio, or \f[CR]No\f[R] otherwise.
Used to enable or disable the modem73 interface.
.TP
\f[B]ET_RETICULUM_INTERFACE_RNODE_ENABLED\f[R]
Replaced with \f[CR]Yes\f[R] when EmComm Tools detects a connected,
supported LoRa device, or \f[CR]No\f[R] otherwise.
Used to enable or disable the Reticulum RNode interface.
.TP
\f[B]ET_RETICULUM_INTERFACE_RNODE_TXPOWER\f[R]
Replaced with the maximum transmit power (dBm) reported by a connected,
supported LoRa device.
Typically used to set the \f[CR]txpower\f[R] parameter of the Reticulum
\f[CR]RNodeInterface\f[R].
.SH RADIO MODEMS
When a supported radio is detected, the following modem selections may
be available, depending on the selected blueprint:
.TP
\f[B]AX.25 Packet\f[R]
1200\-baud VHF/UHF packet or 300\-baud HF packet using Dire Wolf.
.TP
\f[B]modem73\f[R]
Reliability (BPSK), balanced (QPSK), fast (8PSK), faster (QAM16), or
fastest (QAM64).
.TP
\f[B]Mercury HF\f[R]
Mercury broadcast mode.
.PP
The utility starts the selected modem service before launching
Reticulum.
Modem choices are not shown when no supported radio is detected.
.SH PLUG\-AND\-PLAY
\f[B]et\-reticulum\f[R] enables or disables configured modem73, Mercury
HF, AX.25 KISS, and RNode interfaces according to device or service
availability.
For a detected RNode, it queries the maximum transmit power.
The configured fallback is 17 dBm if the query fails.
.PP
The operator callsign is read from EmComm Tools user configuration.
Use \f[B]et\-user\f[R] to change it rather than editing that file
directly.
.SH RETICULUM APPLICATIONS
Once the Reticulum shared instance is running, the operator may start
one or more Reticulum applications.
These applications share the same network interfaces and connectivity
provided by \f[B]rnsd\f[R].
.PP
EmComm Tools supports the following Reticulum applications:
.IP \(bu 2
MeshChat
.IP \(bu 2
NomadNet
.IP \(bu 2
LXMD
.IP \(bu 2
Partyline
.PP
Multiple Reticulum applications may run concurrently using the same
shared instance.
.SH EXAMPLES
.IP
.EX
et\-reticulum
.EE
.SH WHEN TO RUN
Run \f[B]et\-reticulum\f[R] when starting Reticulum or switching to a
different Reticulum configuration blueprint.
.PP
Close the current operating mode before changing radio connections.
